# Maintainerr-specific, NON-SECRET config. This file IS committed.
#
# Shared values (PUID/PGID/TZ/CONFIG_ROOT/DATA_ROOT) live in ../../common.env.
#
# Maintainerr holds no secrets in the environment. Every credential it needs
# (Plex token, Jellyfin key, Radarr/Sonarr/Seerr API keys) is entered in its
# own UI and stored in its SQLite database under /opt/data. That database is
# therefore the one piece of this stack that is NOT reproducible from this
# repo — see the backup note in the README.
#
# ⚠️ No DATA_ROOT mount. Maintainerr does not delete files itself. It asks
# Radarr and Sonarr to remove the media record, and they do the file deletion
# using their own mounts. Giving it a media mount would be handing it a
# capability it does not use.

# Nothing else Maintainerr-specific needed yet.
